{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/906157-beast-and-heroes-in-japan-kaiju-and-tokusatsu-heroes","id":906157,"title":"Beast and Heroes in Japan = Kaiju...and Tokusatsu Heroes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-02T20:26:57-07:00","id":906157,"title":"Beast and Heroes in Japan = Kaiju...and Tokusatsu Heroes?","content":"So reading through the Tokyo setting write up in the corebook, when it comes to Beast it's unique point is the abundance of Heroes. To the point that the Begotten refer to Tokyo as &quot;Hero Bay&quot;. Naturally, the write up doesn't provide a clear cut answer on how and why so many Heroes are attracted to Japan (leaving it up to the Storyteller). But otherwise, not much else on why there just happens to be so many Heroes.<br /> <br /> Now considering that the culture and socio-politics of the region can and does make its way back to the supernaturals. So how would the idea of a high number of individuals who fight primordial monsters come from when it comes to Japan. <br /> <br /> And then it hit me that we do: tokusatsu. <br /> <br /> Tokusatsu, as the West knows it, is a genre of movies and TV exclusively in East Asian media, but has origins (and is most prolific) in Japan. In Japanese the term literally means &quot;special effects&quot; outside of Japan its associated with very specific special effects technique. In the beginning, when it was just kaiju movies, it was of sticking a guy in a rubber suit, build a set of miniatures made to look like a city, and film that actor in such a way to make it appear to be a giant monster stomping a city.<br /> <br /> Later on a new sub-genre would appear, &quot;tokusatsu heroes&quot;. They are just as widespread and popular over there as DC and Marvel superheroes are in America. While it varies from show to show, these heroes usually have some sort of method of transforming into their superhero personas through some kind of device. Their superhero persona, unlike Western heroes, has a costume that usually completely covers their body. Including their face. Which usually means full face helmets. Of course the thing that they are the most known and parodied for is the over the top posing and catch phrases, usually followed by explosions behind them. These kind of characters include Ultraman, Kamen Rider, Metal Heroes, and Super Sentai. <br /> <br /> Although in the West, people would commonly know them as these guys: <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.ew.com/sites/default/files/styles/tout_image_612x380/public/i/2014/08/13/Power-Rangers.jpg?itok=cUB7M5sr\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Godzilla has been stated before as being one of the overall influences of Beast. What with the whole metaphor on the fear of nuclear devastation. Aside from being a landmark film in Japanese cinema and being a cultural icon, the other thing about is starting the tokusatsu genre. Either copycats like Gamera, or expansions on the genre with supeheroes like Ultraman.<br /> <br /> So if you consider the more meta way of looking at it: monsters have arrived terrorizing the island nation, and now heroes among its citizens must rise to fight them. <br /> <br /> Is that what they're going with? Because if so, now I'm going to have hella fun trying to depict Beasts and Heroes in a tokusatsu framing. Especially taking the more broody and lone vigilante tone the book describes Heroes as and a more cheesy and sillier outlook with more naive views of &quot;justice&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T07:49:08-07:00","id":906408,"title":"","content":"Shujinko can also mean Protagonist, which... doesn't sound all that out there for Japanese Heroes to call themselves, particularly if they're at least a little bit of the nerd variety.<br /> <br /> The thought of Heroes acting like they're in a typical Tokusatsu despite everything around them behaving realistically is both amusing and grim to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T08:40:13-07:00","id":906433,"title":"","content":"There are so many ways that I am about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T09:54:34-07:00","id":906492,"title":"","content":"TO remind of a crossover bit, Werewolves regularly fight kaiju Magath, and where the Beasts make friends, the Hero Guilds follow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:19:47-07:00","id":906575,"title":"","content":"And just considering that Hero Guilds are even a thing suggests that Japanese Heroes are stable enough to consider working together for longer periods of time. <br /> <br /> Which opens the door for a Guild considering itself to be like a Super Sentai/Power Rangers team. And while generally these teams are stable enough that stuff like this doesn't happen as much: <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.cosmicbooknews.com/sites/default/files/civilwarintposer.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> When it does happen, well mostly the usual &quot;Why is HE the Red Ranger when I'm SO much more qualified?!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:50:48-07:00","id":906600,"title":"","content":"Well the Leviathans are probably hunted with extreme prejudice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/906157-beast-and-heroes-in-japan-kaiju-and-tokusatsu-heroes?p=906408#post906408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thought of Heroes acting like they're in a typical Tokusatsu despite everything around them behaving realistically is both amusing and grim to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh god, yes, I want the Beast players to run into the Sailor Scouts! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-03-2016, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T10:39:01-07:00","id":907172,"title":"","content":"And now you're making me think of Sin Eaters standing in for the Imagin of Kamen Rider Den-O. XD Still, I love this train of thought.<br /> <br /> However, what about this line of thought: I've noted before that Beasts' Atavisms can easily be made into conventional superpowers for some admittedly anti-superheros, and Beasts do have some investment in keeping humans alive given, well, that's their primary/only real foodsource. Now imagine what a few Heroes may do to &quot;liberate&quot; the people from their &quot;dark oppressors&quot;? You have one side fighting for their glory and purported sanity, whereas the other side is fighting for surviving their own hunger and relative sanity, with humanity caught in the middle. Both sides are a danger to the people they're protecting, but for different reasons, and it's hard to tell which is the lesser of the many evils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T12:15:27-07:00","id":907223,"title":"","content":"Man, I really need to get around to writing up Godzilla.<br /> <br /> In the mean time, have this <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/i-remember-my-heroes\" target=\"_blank\"><b>highly relevant Foundation Tale.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T19:50:06-07:00","id":907393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon 